@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Classic backport policy
+
+## Rules
+
+1. Never merge `upstream` wholesale into `main`.
+2. Review upstream changes by touched paths and actual diff, not by PR/commit title alone.
+3. Prefer backend-only changes under `UniGetUI.Core.*`, `UniGetUI.PackageEngine.*`, and manager projects.
+4. For mixed Avalonia/backend changes, split the backend portion and manually adapt WinUI only when the behavior matters to Classic.
+5. Record every imported upstream change in `maintenance/backports.yml`.
+6. Preserve upstream commit identity in commit messages with `Upstream-Commit:` and `Upstream-PR:` trailers.
+7. Keep Classic-only compatibility code thin. If compatibility changes begin duplicating PackageEngine or manager implementations, stop and reconsider the boundary.
+8. Security fixes outrank feature parity. Backend correctness fixes outrank new UI features.
+9. Avalonia-only appearance, navigation, cross-platform, and NativeAOT changes are non-applicable unless they expose a shared backend defect.
+10. Before every Classic release, review all upstream commits since the last reviewed upstream tag and explicitly classify security-sensitive changes.
+
+## Backport status values
+
+- `candidate`: expected to apply substantially as-is.
+- `partial`: split backend/shared changes from upstream UI changes.
+- `inspect-classic`: upstream fix is UI-specific; first verify Classic has the same defect.
+- `included`: present in Classic.
+- `skipped`: intentionally not applicable; retain the reason.
+
+## Commit message convention
+
+```text
+backport: fix WinGet phantom updates
+
+Upstream-Commit: 26c93b859babdc831b2d8462048d3e5f85d3da67
+Upstream-PR: Devolutions/UniGetUI#5199
+```
+
+The goal is reproducibility: a maintainer should be able to answer exactly which upstream fixes Classic contains without reconstructing Git archaeology.
diff --git a/maintenance/backports.yml b/maintenance/backports.yml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..d721e4fda
--- /dev/null
+++ b/maintenance/backports.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+upstream_base:
+  tag: v2026.2.1
+  commit: 68411409d001b9f34cfb896af1543a1d7067ca5e
+
+backports:
+  - commit: 21116375c8299d1db38a3c3b4c2eb7e18bc97c4e
+    upstream_pr: 5072
+    status: applied
+    class: backend
+    reason: WinGet already-upgraded cache fix; package-engine only plus tests.
+
+  - commit: 905bcd14ab6ac7ffa4e712889c7c34c12f30309f
+    upstream_pr: 5173
+    status: applied-semantic
+    class: backend-shared-model
+    reason: Honors explicit per-package install location on WinGet update; adapted to Classic's inline location logic.
+
+  - commit: c0ddaa670523bd69fa5a036b3c18b2e96fb9c665
+    upstream_pr: 5169
+    status: applied
+    class: backend
+    reason: Preserves PowerShell module scope during update discovery.
+
+  - commit: 4ca6074f301ffb5ea9b2ceb39bd87b814c1a973d
+    upstream_pr: 5167
+    status: applied-backend
+    class: backend-plus-ui
+    reason: Stuck-upgrade detection, settings storage, language, and backend behavior are applied; the Avalonia settings control is intentionally excluded from Classic. Classic currently uses the backend default threshold of 3.
+
+  - commit: 249cc4d0d4c947dbe03b998ff392933f8aab15b6
+    upstream_pr: 4998
+    status: applied-semantic
+    class: backend
+    reason: Retries WinGet/Pinget updates reported as not applicable once without forced scope/architecture, then reports a real failure instead of faking success.
+
+  - commit: 26c93b859babdc831b2d8462048d3e5f85d3da67
+    upstream_pr: 5199
+    status: applied-semantic
+    class: backend
+    depends_on:
+      - 4ca6074f301ffb5ea9b2ceb39bd87b814c1a973d
+      - 249cc4d0d4c947dbe03b998ff392933f8aab15b6
+    reason: Suppresses non-applicable WinGet COM phantom updates using stuck-upgrade tracking after the relaxed not-applicable retry path has been exhausted.
+
+  - commit: fce15a3b10e630b269ce6e59be3c6522e3b0ea94
+    upstream_pr: 5114
+    status: applied-semantic
+    class: backend-plus-ui
+    reason: PowerShell scope handling and operation-specific capabilities are backported with upstream regression tests; Avalonia ScopeEnabled behavior is translated to the Classic WinUI scope selector.
+
+  - commit: 9ae64515163e2d1021301ff48e4c47435b7da1f0
+    upstream_pr: 5077
+    status: skipped
+    class: avalonia-orchestration
+    reason: Avalonia-only regression. Classic's UninstallThenReinstall and UninstallThenUpdate already chain one InstallPackageOperation behind the uninstall prerequisite and do not launch the uninstall separately, so neither #5077 defect is present.
+
+  - commit: 4bcd5d0c2a84884dd07eb2eb90732864c3be00fe
+    upstream_pr: 4959
+    status: applied-semantic
+    class: frontend-selection
+    reason: Upstream retired the Classic frontend entirely. Classic preserves WinUI as its sole frontend, so the semantic backport removes the obsolete UseClassicMode selector while retaining legacy settings and launcher helpers for compatibility and lower maintenance delta.
+
+downstream_patches:
+  - id: sqlitepclraw-ghsa-2m69-gcr7-jv3q
+    issue: 5
+    status: applied
+    class: security-hardening
+    reason: Overrides the SQLitePCLRaw bundle to 2.1.13 because Pinget 0.9.0 transitively resolves vulnerable SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3 2.1.11 through Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.7. Keep only until upstream or Pinget removes the vulnerable resolution.
